to come from the huts (neya) of herders at the foot of Mount Ikoma in ancient times.","和泉市":"The merger application says it plainly: the new city lay at the heart of ancient Izumi Province, so it took the province's name.","守口市":"The tale that it was Hideyoshi's \"guard gate\" for Osaka Castle is folklore. The city history finds both 森口 (\"forest mouth\", the way into woods running toward Mount Ikoma) and 守口 in Muromachi times; the military spelling won out with Ishiyama Hongan-ji and Osaka Castle.","貝塚市":"Once written 海塚 (\"sea mound\"); by the time the Ikkō sect built its temple town in the late 16th century it was 貝塚 (\"shell mound\"). The surrounding old village is still Umizuka. No actual shell middens have been found here."}},"kyu":{"27102":{"t":8,"k":3419,"r":[["@bakufu",3419]]},"27103":{"t":7,"k":4669,"r":[["@bakufu",4669]]},"27104":{"t":14,"k":2201,"r":[["@bakufu",2201]]},"27106":{"t":2,"k":1631,"r":[["@bakufu",1631]]},"27107":{"t":10,"k":2342,"r":[["@bakufu",2342]]},"27108":{"t":15,"k":2031,"r":[["@bakufu",2031]]},"27109":{"t":5,"k":1405,"r":[["Odawara Domain",815],["@bakufu",589],["@other",1]]},"27111":{"t":7,"k":6643,"r":[["@bakufu",6322],["@jisha",321]],"p":1},"27113":{"t":18,"k":7594,"r":[["@bakufu",7594]]},"27114":{"t":16,"k":7141,"r":[["@bakufu",4405],["Koga Domain",1463],["@hatamoto",846],["田安家領",426],["@other",1]]},"27115":{"t":8,"k":4355,"r":[["@bakufu",4095],["Takatsuki Domain",260]]},"27116":{"t":15,"k":7349,"r":[["@bakufu",4006],["Yodo Domain",2491],["Odawara Domain",852]],"p":1},"27117":{"t":12,"k":7107,"r":[["@bakufu",7107]]},"27118":{"t":11,"k":5758,"r":[["@bakufu",5055],["@hatamoto",703]]},"27119":{"t":2,"k":501,"r":[["Odawara Domain",403],["Koga Domain",98]]},"27120":{"t":20,"k":9146,"r":[["Odawara Domain",4916],["@jisha",1471],["@bakufu",1154],["@hatamoto",896],["@other",709]]},"27121":{"t":11,"k":6373,"r":[["@bakufu",2937],["Sayama Domain",1248],["@hatamoto",974],["Koga Domain",686],["@other",528]]},"27122":{"t":2,"k":1885,"r":[["@bakufu